<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Edzard, Prince of East Frisia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1716–1744</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Edzard was the last prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-frisia">East Frisia</a> of the Cirksena dynasty, ruling from 1734 to 1744. His reign was troubled by conflict with the East Frisian estates and the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emden">Emden</a>. When he died without heirs in 1744, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick II of Prussia</a> occupied East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frisia">Frisia</a> under a succession right granted by the emperor, and the principality became a Prussian province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-edzard-prince-of-east-frisia.jpg" alt="Charles Edzard, Prince of East Frisia" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Not mentioned · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carl_Edzard_(F%C3%BCrst_von_Ostfriesland)_%E2%80%93_Portr%C3%A4t_im_Besitz_der_Ostfriesischen_Landschaft_(18._Jh.).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
